    "title": "September 26, 1970 - The Apostle Islands become Wisconsin's first national lakeshore - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Alaina Tomesh ,\n21 hours ago MADISON, Wis. (WMTV) - On this day, September 26, 1970, the Apostle Islands became Wisconsin’s first national lakeshore, located off the shore of northern Wisconsin in Lake Superior. The Apostle Islands are a group of 22 islands known for their stunning sea caves and historic lighthouses. The largest island,... Read full article\n4",
